{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103744","id":2377625133,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6Nt64t","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103744.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103744/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103744/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103744/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e95908fac93ff0d8d01290bbdcca04f39f5a3ecc","number":103744,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add virtual joypad buttons for semantic \"yes\"/\"no\"","user":{"login":"Grublady","id":29121925,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MTIxOTI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29121925?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady","html_url":"https://github.com/Grublady","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Grublady/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR adds \"virtual\" joypad buttons which correspond to *semantic* inputs rather than *physical* inputs.\r\n\r\nThese virtual button events can be mapped to actions as usual, allowing interface actions such as \"confirm\" or \"cancel\" to use any supported controller's native semantics.\r\n\r\nFor example, although the `A` buttons on Xbox and Switch controllers send `JoyButton::A` and `JoyButton::B` respectively, both inputs would now also send `JoyButton::SEMANTIC_YES` as well.\r\n\r\nTested on macOS 15.3 with Switch Pro Controller and Switch Joy-Cons, needs testing on other platforms/controllers.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nPreviously, joypad face button events were identified strictly by position (ie top, bottom, left, right).\r\nThis is typically desirable for gameplay, as the control layout can be designed once and keep the same ergonomics across controllers.\r\n\r\nHowever, this system created a problem when accounting for controller layouts whose face button semantics are reversed:\r\nFor example, Xbox controllers use the **bottom** (`A`) button for \"yes,\" \"confirm,\" or \"select\" in menu navigation, whereas Switch controllers use the **right** (`A`) button for these purposes.\r\nThus, mapping one of these face button positions to menu navigation is always unintuitive for some controllers.\r\n\r\nThe goal of this PR is to allow developers to easily implement semantically-correct interaction.\r\nThis is relevant to most games, so I believe it makes sense as an engine feature.","labels":[{"id":73330068,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2OA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/feature%20proposal","name":"feature proposal","description":"","color":"4466ff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"h